# Claude harness runtime state — verdicts are per-checkout, not shared history.
# ONLY the state directory: `.claude/` as a whole would untrack the rules, agents,
# hooks, skills and settings, which are checked-in shared configuration. Git keeps
# already-tracked files tracked, so the wider pattern did not delete anything — it
# silently stopped new harness files being added, and broke `git add` partway through
# a commit, which is how the rules consolidation ended up half-staged.
.claude/state/
.agents
